/target
# packaging/verify-deb.sh and packaging/verify-rpm.sh build inside a
# container, which cannot share /target with the host: the host's artifacts
# are linked against a different glibc. Each gets its own directory under
# the checkout, and each is gigabytes of build output that a careless
# `git add .` would otherwise stage.
/target-debian
/target-fedora
*.log

# iscc writes the compiled installer here, both in CI and when the script is
# compiled locally (Inno Setup runs under wine, which is how the compile is
# checked without a Windows machine). OutputDir in pheme.iss names it.
/packaging/windows/Output
